Z||000000||WampusCat||12-06-2000||04:54 PM||||The 88GT I bought has fairly worn rear tires and I plan to replace them soon but the fronts are brand new 205-60R15's called "Douglas performance GT-H"  The DOT code is from the Kelly Springfield plant in NC but I've never heard of this brand.  Is anyone familiar with these?  Are they worth keeping?  I'd hate to replace NEW tires.  Also any recommendations for tires in stock sizes for a GT would be appreciated.<P>Steve||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||12-06-2000||06:05 PM||||Seems like I remember hearing about Douglas tires, a long time ago. Don't know much about them. I wouldn't trash 'em, though, unless you just don't like them or unless they cause problems. <BR>My next tires will be BF Goodrich. <BR>My Goodyears (even the second set) suck. Loudly. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DougV||12-06-2000||06:37 PM||||I have been using Firestone(No jokes please, I work for them!) Firehawk SH30 tires on my 86 GT(205/60, 215/60) Great dry and wet weather tire. Very quiet and good wear. I got about 45k miles on the rear and still running the fronts after 4 years. They are about $80 each for the front, $85 each for the back. A real Nice looking tire as well. Another good choice would be the Bridgestone RE930. Any guys local to NJ could come to my shop and I could get you a lower price.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WampusCat||12-06-2000||08:41 PM||||My wife has Firehawk SZ50's on her Mustang GT and they are great but unfortunately, they don't come in sizes for the Fiero.  Also, they're really expensive.  Have to look into those SH30's.||||reg||1
Z||000004||jerpro||12-07-2000||02:38 AM||||best tires are goodyear's gt road huggers.<BR>they stick llike glue||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||12-07-2000||02:42 AM||||BFGoodrich. The only tires I will use. I have tried Goodyears, Firestones, and Pirelli's. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||12-07-2000||06:49 AM||||while i have never owned a car with Douglas Tires, i have heard of them.  it is very possible that they were made for a several NC chains.  <P>if you like there look and feel, i wouldnt worry about em!<P>hoop||||reg||2
Z||000007||WMEBERT||05-30-2001||08:33 PM||||I know this is an old post but I was searching for tire fitment advice and stumbled upon it.  Douglas Tires are sold by Wal-Mart.  I've had them on a Mazda RX-7 'vert and an '84 Trans Am and have had good luck with them.  They aren't "performance tires" but they're just fine for a daily driver.<P>Bill<BR>86.5 GT<BR>2001 Crown Vic<BR>96 S10 Blazer||||reg||6
